window.__CAPS = [[0.35, 6.0, "Project controls is the discipline\nthat turns intent into delivery."], [6.0, 16.1, "Planning, cost, earned value, forecasting,\nrisk and project finance \u2014 practised as one\nintegrated whole, not as separate techniques."], [16.72, 25.67, "Project management has PMI.\nAccountancy has ACCA. Finance has CFA."], [25.67, 32.15, "Project controls has had no equivalent \u2014 no\nshared standard, and no professional home."], [32.77, 40.04, "And the discipline is changing. Schedules, forecasts\nand cost reports are increasingly supported by AI."], [40.04, 49.25, "It can accelerate analysis. It can also create false\nconfidence. Technology does not remove accountability."], [49.87, 62.26, "PCI AI exists to close that gap: to give\nproject controls a shared standard, an\nindependent credential and a professional home."], [62.26, 68.32, "Built for how the discipline is practised\nnow, with AI governance at its core."], [68.94, 80.11, "Its mission is to advance the profession through\ncertification, research, professional development,\nstandards, publications and the responsible adoption\nof AI."], [80.73, 88.73, "Its position on that adoption is\nexplicit. It certifies professionals\nwho govern AI \u2014 not who defer to it."], [89.35, 97.27, "The framework is the PCI AI Project\nLeadership Certification Suite \u2014\nthree AI-era leadership credentials."], [97.89, 110.6, "PCL-AI, for project controls. PFL-AI, for\nproject finance. PML-AI, for project management."], [110.6, 116.13, "Finance intelligently. Control\npredictively. Deliver successfully."], [116.75, 120.36, "Each credential rests on a\npublished Body of Knowledge."], [120.36, 128.27, "Its first edition defines thirteen\ndomains and sixty-one knowledge\nareas, weighted forty, forty, twenty."], [128.89, 132.89, "Project accounting and finance. Project\nmanagement principles. And governed AI."], [132.89, 142.65, "AI is not an appendix. It is a domain in its own\nright, and it is embedded through the other twelve."], [143.27, 147.17, "The examination is scenario-based\nand criterion-referenced."], [147.17, 159.59, "It asks whether you can read a cost position,\ninterpret an earned-value index, judge a risk\nresponse, and decide whether an AI-generated forecast\ncan be trusted."], [160.21, 165.98, "There are two routes in \u2014 an experience route\nfor practitioners, and a Foundation route."], [165.98, 175.47, "The credential renews on a three-year CPD\ncycle with a mandatory AI-currency component,\nand every credential can be verified publicly."], [176.09, 187.19, "The discipline is the same wherever\ncapital is deployed at scale, so the\ncredential is written to travel."], [187.19, 195.3, "Energy and utilities. Rail and\ntransportation. Aerospace and defence. Oil\nand gas. Construction and infrastructure."], [195.3, 199.78, "Aviation. Manufacturing. Data centres.\nSmart cities. And government programmes."], [200.4, 210.82, "For organisations, the same standard supports team\nenrolment at scale through corporate programmes, and\ncurriculum alignment through university partnerships."], [211.44, 228.61, "PCI is candid about what it is not.\nIt is not accredited by ANAB, IAS, or\nany ISO/IEC 17024 accreditation body."], [228.61, 234.19, "Its framework is developed with reference\nto those personnel-certification\nprinciples, and it says so plainly."], [234.19, 244.14, "For a body whose value rests on trust, that\nrestraint is the foundation \u2014 not a weakness."], [244.76, 248.97, "AI proposes. The professional disposes."], [248.97, 255.14, "Discover PCI AI at pciai.org"]];
